        "title": "Minimum Spanning Trees",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "A minimum spanning tree (MST) connects all V vertices of a weighted, *undirected*,\n*connected* graph using V−1 edges of minimum total weight. The remarkable fact is\nthat the obvious greedy strategies — Prim's \"grow from a seed\" and Kruskal's \"add\ncheapest safe edge\" — both provably produce an MST. The reason is two structural\ntheorems (the cut property and the cycle property), and understanding *those* is\nthe real content; the algorithms are corollaries."
    }
